# The project video, as a cue sheet.
#
# Every frame is the real plugin rendering through the real FFGL sequence -- this
# is the generator being *operated*, not a mock-up. Render with:
#
#   ./build/ortest --sequence /tmp/or-frames --script tools/video.cues \
#                  --size 1920x1080 --seconds 45 --fps 30
#
# Syntax: `T Name=V` sets at a time, `T1..T2 Name=V1..V2` ramps between two
# (eased, because a parameter that starts and stops abruptly reads as a cut).
#
# Every value here is the 0..1 the host sees, not the physical quantity -- see
# Controls.h for why there is no other kind. The physical value each one lands on
# is in the comment where it matters.
#
# The order of the piece is the order of the argument: a mask first, because that
# is the simplest thing it does; then what the shapes can be; then where they can
# go; and the pixel-map grid last, because that is the thing worth staying for.

# ------------------------------------------------------------ 0s: a mask
# White circles on black, orbiting. No colour yet, nothing clever -- this is
# what somebody wants at 2am when they need a moving mask and do not want to
# open an animation package.
0.0   Path=0
0.0   Shape=0
0.0   Colour Mode=0
0.0   Speed=0.52
0.0   Size=0.66
0.0   Path Size=0.50
0.0   Spread=1.0
0.0   Background Opacity=1.0

# Open on three and fill in, so the first thing the eye gets is a chase it can
# count rather than a crowd.
0.0..6.0    Count=0.20..0.40

# ------------------------------------------------- 6s: colour, and the chase
# Hue Spread is the parameter that turns a mask into a pixel-map chase, so it
# gets its own moment before anything else moves.
6.0   Colour Mode=2
6.0   Hue Spread=1.0
6.0..11.0   Count=0.40..0.52
6.0..11.0   Size=0.66..0.60

# --------------------------------------------------------- 12s: the shapes
# Cuts, not ramps: Shape is a dropdown and pretending otherwise would be a lie
# about what the control does.
12.0  Shape=1
13.5  Shape=2
15.0  Shape=3
16.5  Shape=4

# The outline rides across the shape changes to show it is one control that
# works on all of them, not eight sets of geometry.
12.0..15.0  Outline=0.0..0.30
15.0..18.0  Outline=0.30..0.0
12.0..18.0  Spin=0.50..0.62

# ------------------------------------------------------ 18s: Lissajous
# Two ratios, and a path that stops repeating the moment they are not whole
# numbers. Ramping Ratio X off 3 is the whole point of the section.
18.0  Path=1
18.0  Shape=0
18.0  Spin=0.50
# 1:2 -- a figure of eight -- and NOT the 3:2 this section first used.
#
# A Lissajous is a curve, and the shapes are point samples of it, so the figure
# is only legible while consecutive instances are close enough together to read
# as a line. The arc length grows with the ratios, and at 3:2 even all 64
# instances land as a scatter of dots that happen to be moving: correct, and
# completely unreadable. 1:2 is the highest-order figure that still draws itself
# at this instance count.
18.0  Ratio X=0.25
18.0  Ratio Y=0.50
18.0..20.0  Count=0.52..1.0
18.0..20.0  Size=0.60..0.39
18.0..20.0  Path Size=0.50..0.62

# Now push Ratio X a little off the whole number. The figure stops closing and
# starts precessing, which is the claim the README makes about this control and
# the one thing worth showing about it.
20.0..26.0  Ratio X=0.25..0.32
20.0..26.0  Speed=0.52..0.60

# ----------------------------------------------------------- 26s: Drift
# Bars crossing the frame at a heading. This is the wipe, and it is also what a
# chase across a truss looks like from the pixel mapper's side.
26.0  Path=2
26.0  Shape=7
26.0  Stretch=0.70
26.0  Spin=0.50
26.0  Count=0.42
26.0  Size=0.60
26.0  Path Size=0.62
26.0  Direction=0.0
26.0..32.0  Direction=0.0..0.14

# ---------------------------------------------------------- 32s: Bounce
# Scatter is the difference between one path many shapes are chasing round and
# many shapes going their own way, so it ramps rather than cuts.
32.0  Path=3
32.0  Shape=1
32.0  Stretch=0.50
32.0  Roundness=0.20
32.0  Outline=0.22
32.0  Count=0.34
32.0  Size=0.66
32.0  Path Size=0.67
32.0  Ratio X=0.55
32.0  Ratio Y=0.62
32.0..37.0  Scatter=0.0..0.85

# ------------------------------------------------------- 37s: the pixel map
# The payoff, and the reason the plugin exists. A fixture grid, one hue per
# fixture, pulsing on the beat -- the shapes have stopped being graphics.
37.0  Path=4
37.0  Shape=0
37.0  Outline=0.0
37.0  Roundness=0.0
37.0  Scatter=0.0
37.0  Grid Columns=0.60
37.0  Grid Rows=0.333
37.0  Count=0.968
37.0  Size=0.52
37.0  Path Size=0.64
37.0  Pulse Width=0.50
37.0..40.0  Pulse Size=0.0..0.55
37.0..40.0  Speed=0.60..0.52

# Settle into a steady chase for the last few seconds rather than ending on a
# transition -- the last frame is the one that gets used as a still.
40.0..45.0  Pulse Size=0.55..0.42
